ct-flagship1.jpg?aio=w-725;h-350;crop;)\n![Vainganga Apartment Tower View](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/vainganga-apartment-project-tower-view1.jpg?aio=w-192;h-168;crop;)\n\n**₹61,364 Per Sq. Ft Onwards**\n\n₹61,364 Per Sq. Ft.\n\n## Why Invest Through Square Yards?\n\n![Zero brokerage icon](/assets/images/zero-brokerage.svg)\n\n### Zero Brokerage\n\n100% Service, 0% Brokerage\n\n![Lowest price icon](/assets/images/lowest-price.svg)\n\n### Lowest Price Guaranteed\n\nHighly unlikely, but if you find a lower price anywhere, tell us and we will match it.\n\n![Full service support icon](/assets/images/full-service-support.svg)\n\n### Full Service Support\n\nOur sales personnel are accountable for every step.\n\n## About Vainganga Apartment, Worli by\n\n## Vainganga Apartment Price List, Price Trends and Market Insights\n\n### Price List\n\nView the latest price list for Vainganga Apartment.\n\n| Unit Type (BuiltUp) | Price\\* | Action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 BHK Apartment  1160 Sq. Ft. | **Price on Request** | Check Availability |\n\n\\*Prices are indicative and subject to applicable charges and project terms.\n\n### Price Trends\n\nVainganga Apartment's average asking price is rising quarter-on-quarter, compared with Worli.\n\nSep 2025 — Jun 2026\n\n| Quarter | Vainganga Apartment | Worli |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Jun 2026 | 50950 | 66500 |\n| Mar 2026 | 48400 | 74050 |\n| Dec 2025 | 43750 | 70800 |\n| Sep 2025 | 46100 | 65700 |\n\n### Comparable Projects\n\nVainganga Apartment avg. price is ₹ 51 K/Sq.Ft. compared to Worli at ₹ 66.5 K/Sq.Ft.\n\n| Project | Avg. ₹/sq ft |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Piramal Mahalaxmi](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/piramal-mahalaxmi/10037/project \"Piramal Mahalaxmi\") | ₹ 71,350 |\n| Worli | ₹ 66,500 |\n| [Prestige Jasdan Classic](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/prestige-jasdan-classic/113126/project \"Prestige Jasdan Classic\") | ₹ 61,400 |\n| Current Project **Vainganga Apartment** | ₹ 50,950 |\n| [Lodha Primo](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/lodha-primo/100289/project \"Lodha Primo\") | ₹ 49,750 |\n\n### Rentals\n\nMonthly Rent in Worli ranges from ₹ 34.9 K to ₹ 9.6 L with options available for STUDIO,1,2,3,4,5,6 BHK units\n\n| Configuration | In Vainganga Apartment | In Worli |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 BHK | - | ₹ 70 K |\n| 2 BHK | - | ₹ 1.9 L |\n| 3 BHK | - | ₹ 3.8 L |\n| 4 BHK | - | ₹ 5.2 L |\n| 5 BHK | - | ₹ 8.7 L |\n| 6 BHK | - | ₹ 9.6 L |\n\n### Recent Updates\n\nGet the latest price and market updates for Vainganga Apartment.\n\nA total of 1 residential transactions has been registered so far for Vainganga Apartment, amounting to ₹ 4 Cr till September 2026.\n\n#### 27 Underground Parking Facilities to Combat Mumbai's Parking Crisis\n\nMumbai is set to develop 27 underground parking facilities, one in each administrative ward, to alleviate the severe parking shortage. This project, backed by the BMC Budget 2026-27, will create parking beneath existing gardens and playgrounds, reducing roadside parking and traffic congestion.\n\n#### New Road Link Approved to Enhance Mumbai Connectivity\n\nThe Maharashtra government has approved a ₹1,722 crore road link project aimed at connecting the Versova-Bandra Sea Link with the Mumbai Coastal Road. This infrastructure development is expected to significantly improve traffic flow, reduce commuting times across the city.\n\nDuring Q2'2026, average property prices for Vainganga Apartment moved from ₹ 48,400/sqft to ₹ 50,950/sqft, reflecting a 5.27% rise.\n\n#### Mumbai to Establish Four New Helipads for Emergency Services\n\nMumbai authorities are planning to construct four new helipads within the next six years to enhance emergency response capabilities. Two helipads will be built along the Coastal Road, one at Worli and another in Kandivali's Charkop area. The remaining two will be developed in the Bandra Kurla Complex (BKC).\n\n#### Elphinstone Road Overbridge Dismantled for Infrastructure Upgrade\n\nMumbai's historic Elphinstone Road Overbridge, a 113-year-old British-era structure, has been dismantled. This move is part of infrastructure upgrades aimed at improving rail operations and commuter safety. The dismantling creates space for two additional suburban lines between Kurla and Parel, which will eventually extend to CSMT. A new double-decker ROB will replace the old structure.\n\n#### Versova Property Market Poised for Growth Driven by Sea Link and Redevelopment\n\nThe Versova property market is experiencing a surge in demand and property prices, fueled by the upcoming Versova-Bandra Sea Link and ongoing redevelopment projects. This infrastructure development is expected to sustain property values and attract significant buyer interest in the coming years.\n\nDuring Q1'2026, average property prices for Vainganga Apartment moved from ₹ 43,750/sqft to ₹ 48,400/sqft, reflecting a 10.63% rise.\n\n#### Mumbai Infrastructure Projects Gain Momentum with Budget Allocations and Project Launches\n\nMumbai is experiencing a surge in infrastructure and activity. The BMC has proposed a record budget of ₹80,952.56 crore for FY 2026-27, with a significant portion allocated to infrastructure projects like the Coastal Road, Goregaon-Mulund Link Road (GMLR), and Sewage Treatment Plants (STPs).MMRDA has allocated over ₹5,400 crore for road tunnel projects, including one connecting Worli-Bandra Sea Link to Mumbai Airport.\n\n#### BMC Outlines Timelines for Key Infrastructure Projects\n\nThe BMC has set completion targets for key infrastructure projects: the Bandra (E)-Kalanagar skywalk (almost complete) , the first phase of the Bandra-Dharavi flyover reconstruction (Mithi river widening project ,near completion) , and the Worli connector by December 2026. These projects are expected to improve pedestrian access, ease traffic congestion, and enhance overall connectivity within the city.\n\n### Govt. Registrations\n\n1